cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Threadfin: clone-level analysis of B-cell states from paired single-cell RNA-seq and BCR-seq"
message: "If you use Threadfin, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Satoshi
    given-names: Chen
    alias: Reynold4k
url: "https://github.com/Reynold4k/Threadfin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Reynold4k/Threadfin"
license: MIT
version: 4.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-03"
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - scRNA-seq
  - BCR
  - B cell
  - clonal lineage
  - germinal centre
  - immunology
abstract: >-
  Threadfin treats each B-cell clone as the unit of analysis in paired
  single-cell RNA-seq and BCR-seq data. This matters most where the biology
  is a cycle, such as a germinal centre, in which cells cannot be ordered but
  clones can be compared with one another. Threadfin defines clones within
  donors, describes each clone relative to the cells it was sampled with,
  measures how much of B-cell state is inherited within clones, groups clones
  only when the split between groups is significant, tests what explains the
  differences between clones with clones as replicates, and measures whether
  clones keep their state over time, across tissues and across the
  compartments of a germinal centre.
